# Solreign easter egg functionality — acid-green corporate voice.

# SolreignEgg15, the wrist-mounted post-apocalyptic organizer: a self-scan readout on use.
solreign-wrist-organizer-readout = WRIST UNIT: vitals { $vitals }. Doom index: { $doom }%.
solreign-wrist-organizer-recalibrating = The wrist unit is still recalibrating from your last check-in.

# Delight-eggs batch (feat/delight-eggs): the wrist unit's readout drifts across its own use count
# this round (SolreignWristOrganizerRules.DriftTierForPriorUses). Tier 0 = second use, tier 1 = third
# use onward.
solreign-wrist-organizer-drift-0-1 = A small addendum scrolls past: your check-in frequency has been noted and logged.
solreign-wrist-organizer-drift-0-2 = A footer line blinks once: this unit does not judge. It only reports.
solreign-wrist-organizer-drift-1-1 = For a moment the readout drops the corporate tone entirely: you really are still standing. Good.
solreign-wrist-organizer-drift-1-2 = The screen holds a beat longer than usual, as if deciding whether to say something. It doesn't.

# Delight-eggs batch: proximity payoff for SolreignEgg19's existing "crackles with static whenever
# bad vibes are nearby" flavor text — a scan on use, gated by SolreignStaticReceiverSystem.
# REDESIGNED per orchestrator round-integrity review 2026-07-16: crackle text is tiered atmosphere
# (two common variants + one rare "almost-words" line, indices matching
# SolreignStaticReceiverRules.CrackleVariant) and deliberately never names a direction, distance,
# or kind of source — the signal is ambiguous and noisy by design, radar copy would oversell it.
solreign-static-receiver-crackle-faint = A faint static washes through the receiver, scratchy and directionless, then thins out again.
solreign-static-receiver-crackle-hum = The receiver settles into a low hum that wasn't there a moment ago. It declines to elaborate.
solreign-static-receiver-crackle-words = For half a second the static almost arranges itself into words. You are fairly sure one of them was yours.
solreign-static-receiver-calm = The receiver murmurs quiet, even static. Or perhaps it's just static.
solreign-static-receiver-recalibrating = The receiver is still hissing through its last scan.

# Delight-eggs batch: SolreignCuriosityExamine escalating examine text — SolreignEgg08 (flask of
# golden grace). Tier 0 (1st look), tier 1 (3rd look), tier 2 (6th look), plus a rare aside.
solreign-egg08-examine-tier0 = The amber fluid catches the light strangely — like it's looking back.
solreign-egg08-examine-tier1 = Reading the cork's tiny print again: "Solreign Grace-Adjacent Beverage Solutions. Side effects may include grace."
solreign-egg08-examine-tier2 = You've studied this flask enough times now that the label's fine print has started to feel personal, somehow.
solreign-egg08-examine-aside = Deep in the glass, for just a moment, the liquid seems to spell out a word in a language you don't recognize. Then it doesn't.

# Delight-eggs batch: SolreignCuriosityExamine escalating examine text — SolreignEgg11
# (high-altitude winged berry, one of the animated eggs). Tier 0/1/2 + a rare aside.
solreign-egg11-examine-tier0 = The wings flutter once, as if startled that you're still looking.
solreign-egg11-examine-tier1 = It drifts a fraction higher every time you check on it. You're fairly sure that isn't wind.
solreign-egg11-examine-tier2 = At this point you're fairly sure the berry is examining you back, on some kind of delay.
solreign-egg11-examine-aside = For one frame, the wingbeat syncs exactly with your own heartbeat. You elect not to think about that further.
